{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0171S9FvGW6MCyFstPHC5eLC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the comprehensive best-tier predictions for all planned experiments.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  全部四条 Claim 以完整力度着陆。\"31% of MMLU Items Are Functionally Unstable\" 作为 discovery paper\n  被接受。评审认可 \"old psychometric method × unprecedented LLM benchmark scale = genuine empirical discovery\"\n  的 novelty 逻辑。IRT misspecification（98% |Lz|>2）被视为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象，作为 honest limitation 处理，\n  指向 multidimensional IRT future work。\"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事清晰，ρ≈0.997 是 strength\n  （massive redundancy），31% 是 diagnostic signal。difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 作为 mechanistic story\n  引起共鸣。GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark evidence，宽 CI 被接受为 honest reporting。\n  reviewer_avg_score: 6.5, acceptance_probability_pct: 68, claims_at_full_strength: 4,\n  novelty_sub_score_avg: 3.0, reviewers_flagging_irt_as_fatal: 0, major_revisions_needed: 0-1。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: Real Data DIF on MMLU (DONE — predict best-tier interpretation)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"real_data_dif_mmlu\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      MH-DIF applied to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 items).\n      Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family confound control,\n      domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n      temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.318\n      temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n      ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n      ability_enrichment: 1.19\n      within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n      domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n      domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n      sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n      temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，31.3% temporal C% 被评审接受为 genuine empirical discovery——这是首次对 LLM benchmark\n      做如此大规模的 DIF 分析。enrichment≈0.96 不再被解读为 \"DIF 失败\"，而是完美支撑 Claim 2 的 meta-critique：\n      Li et al. web-overlap labels 测量的是 global exposure，不是 differential contamination，因此\n      enrichment≈1.0 是 expected。random split 0.18% 彻底排除统计伪像。domain ρ=0.307 是 modest\n      ecological correlation，但 plan_019 的 item-level decomposition（≤2.4pp/7.6%）证明 instability\n      是 predominantly item-specific，不是 \"models got better\" 的 proxy。评审认可这组结果的 completeness\n      和 methodological rigor（4-way sensitivity matrix + sanity checks）。A1 假设成立：ML 评审接受\n      \"established psychometric method at unprecedented scale\" 的 novelty 逻辑。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary\"\n        columns: [cohort_definition, N_ref, N_foc, ETS_A_pct, ETS_B_pct, ETS_C_pct, enrichment_vs_Li]\n        rows:\n          - [temporal_2023v2024, 1253, 656, 45.2, 23.5, 31.3, 0.96]\n          - [ability_quintile, 2613, 2614, 90.8, 6.3, 2.9, 1.19]\n          - [random_split_sanity, 2613, 2614, 99.6, 0.2, 0.18, \"N/A\"]\n      - name: \"Table 2: Domain-Specificity (57 subjects)\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [C%_range, \"20.7–48.4%\"]\n          - [unweighted_mean, \"~30%\"]\n          - [ρ_vs_accuracy_improvement, 0.307]\n          - [p_value, 0.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Heatmap of 57-subject C% sorted by domain cluster. All subjects show >20% C%. Color gradient from green (20%) to red (48%).\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Scatter plot of subject-level C% vs accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307). Modest positive trend, large residual variance emphasizes item-specific drivers.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_001 provides the headline finding. In best tier, the pivot from \"contamination detector\"\n      to \"benchmark characterization\" is complete and compelling. The 31.3% figure survives all\n      robustness checks (plans 018, 019, 020, 022). Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% is reframed\n      as evidence of genuine capability evolution, not a confound. Two reviewers note the thoroughness\n      of the multi-cohort design; one asks about non-uniform DIF (addressed by plan_021).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: RL Robustness Validation (PLANNED — not in registry)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"rl_robustness_validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      Validate DIF robustness to RL training: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477),\n      10-15 reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO) added to focal cohort. Compare DIF retention vs\n      traditional detector (Min-K%, ConStat) degradation on RL models.\n    expected_results:\n      sft_baseline_c_pct: 30.8\n      alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct: 31.1\n      reasoning_rl_mixed_cohort_c_pct: 30.5\n      jaccard_sft_vs_alignment_rl: 0.89\n      jaccard_sft_vs_reasoning_rl_mixed: 0.86\n      dif_retention_ratio: 0.97\n      constat_auroc_sft: 0.72\n      constat_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.41\n      mink_auroc_sft: 0.68\n      mink_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.35\n      tost_equivalence_p: 0.008\n      bootstrap_ci_dif_retention: [0.93, 1.01]\n      n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，DIF 的 group-level 设计天然免疫 RL。MH-DIF 在 matched-score strata 内比较 item\n      通过率——它不依赖单个模型的 NLL 分布（Min-K%）或 perturbation 响应（ConStat），因此 RL 训练后的 NLL gap\n      contraction 和 generation distribution 变化不影响 DIF。A1 假设成立：评审理解 DIF 是 group-level\n      统计量，13 个 RL 模型混入 ~800+ focal cohort 不会改变 strata 构成。SFT vs alignment-RL Jaccard=0.89\n      反映 DPO/ORPO 不改变 item functioning。ConStat/Min-K% AUROC 从 0.68-0.72 降至 0.35-0.41 提供了\n      explicit contrast。TOST 等价性检验 p=0.008 正式确认 DIF retention。但评审可能注意到 N=13 reasoning-RL\n      太少，最多 1 位评审要求更多模型——在 best 档下这被视为 minor concern 而非 fatal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: DIF Robustness to Training Paradigm\"\n        columns: [cohort_composition, N_total, C_pct, Jaccard_vs_SFT, retention_ratio]\n        rows:\n          - [SFT_only, 380, 30.8, 1.00, 1.00]\n          - [alignment_RL_DPO_ORPO, 477, 31.1, 0.89, 0.97]\n          - [mixed_reasoning_RL, 393, 30.5, 0.86, 0.97]\n      - name: \"Table S2: Traditional Detector Degradation\"\n        columns: [detector, AUROC_SFT, AUROC_reasoning_RL, delta, DeLong_p]\n        rows:\n          - [Min-K%, 0.68, 0.35, -0.33, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [ConStat, 0.72, 0.41, -0.31, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [DIF_MH, 0.93, 0.91, -0.02, 0.42]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: ROC curves for DIF vs Min-K% vs ConStat on SFT cohort (left) and reasoning-RL-mixed cohort (right). DIF curves nearly identical; traditional detectors collapse.\"\n    analysis: >\n      In best tier, this experiment lands as appendix-strength supporting evidence. The N=13\n      reasoning-RL limitation is acknowledged transparently. The key result is the contrast:\n      traditional detectors degrade dramatically while DIF is invariant. One reviewer may ask\n      whether DIF would still be robust if the focal cohort were majority RL — acknowledged as\n      future work given current reasoning-RL model scarcity. This experiment is NOT in the main\n      body (paper_framing.md already notes N=13 is underpowered → limitations disclosure, not claim).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003a: ConStat Perturbation Evaluation (PLANNED — dropped from paper)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"constat_perturbation_eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003a\"\n    description: >\n      Independent ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+ MMLU items. Generate paraphrases,\n      compare original vs reformulated performance, apply FDR-controlled detection.\n    expected_results:\n      n_items_paraphrased: 250\n      n_models_tested: 15\n      constat_detection_rate_sft: 0.34\n      constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.08\n      fdr_controlled_detections: 62\n      semantic_equivalence_score: 0.91\n      constat_fpr_on_clean: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，ConStat 在非 RL 模型上展现 moderate detection power（~34%），但在 RL 模型上接近 chance\n      level（~8%），验证了 perturbation-based 方法对 RL 的脆弱性。这为 Claim 2 meta-critique 提供了\n      complementary baseline：ConStat 检测的是 verbatim memorization（对 paraphrase 敏感），而非\n      differential contamination。但 paper_framing.md 已将 plan_003a/b/c 标记为 \"never executed, future work\"，\n      所以即使结果干净，它只出现在 appendix 或 discussion 中作为 \"related method comparison\"。评审不要求\n      这个实验存在——paper 已经 pivoted 到 characterization narrative，不需要 detection method 比较。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S3: ConStat Baseline Performance\"\n        columns: [model_type, N_models, detection_rate, FDR_controlled_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [SFT, 8, 0.34, 27.2]\n          - [DPO/ORPO, 5, 0.21, 14.8]\n          - [reasoning_RL, 2, 0.08, 3.2]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Detection rate by model training paradigm showing ConStat degradation under RL.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dropped from main paper. In best tier, this would have been a clean baseline comparison but\n      is unnecessary for the characterization narrative. If executed, it strengthens the meta-critique\n      (Claim 2) by showing ConStat also can't distinguish web-overlap from differential contamination.\n      Paper framing correctly categorizes this as future work.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003b: DVD Generation Variance Evaluation (PLANNED — dropped from paper)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003b\"\n    description: >\n      DVD generation variance on MMLU: 10-15 open-weight models, 50 responses per item via\n      temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection for contamination.\n    expected_results:\n      n_models: 12\n      n_items_tested: 500\n      bimodal_items_detected: 47\n      dvd_auroc_vs_li_labels: 0.58\n      dvd_auroc_vs_semi_synthetic: 0.63\n      variant_contamination_sensitivity: 0.22\n      verbatim_contamination_sensitivity: 0.51\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，DVD 展现 moderate verbatim contamination sensitivity（0.51）但 variant contamination\n      几乎无效（0.22）。这是 DVD 方法的 known limitation——generation variance 需要 exact memorization\n      才能产生 bimodal 分布，variant contamination 只改变 posterior probability 不产生 bimodality。\n      与 plan_003a 一样，paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"never executed, future work\"。\n      在 best 档下评审不会因为缺少这个实验而扣分——paper 不声称做 detection method 比较。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dropped from main paper. Would have provided variant-contamination detection baseline.\n      Paper narrative has pivoted away from detection → characterization, making this unnecessary\n      for acceptance. Best tier does not require execution.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003c: Ensemble Fusion (PLANNED — dropped from paper)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"ensemble_fusion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003c\"\n    description: >\n      Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble with calibrated thresholds,\n      majority voting, weighted fusion, and cross-validated weights.\n    expected_results:\n      ensemble_tpr_at_fpr010: 0.78\n      ensemble_coverage_complementarity: 0.89\n      dif_unique_detections_pct: 31\n      constat_unique_detections_pct: 18\n      dvd_unique_detections_pct: 7\n      overlap_all_three_pct: 12\n      fusion_auroc: 0.82\n      uniform_weight_auroc: 0.79\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，三信号 ensemble 理论上能覆盖更多 contamination 类型（DIF: differential, ConStat: verbatim,\n      DVD: bimodal），但 paper_framing.md 明确将其标记为 \"never executed, future work\"。\n      Paper 已从 \"detection ensemble\" 彻底转向 \"characterization + meta-critique\"。\n      评审不会因为没有 ensemble 而降分——paper 的 novelty 来自 scale + meta-critique + framework，不是更好的检测器。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Explicitly dropped. Not needed for best-tier acceptance under the current characterization\n      framing. Would only matter if the paper claimed to build a better contamination detector,\n      which it does not.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: Cross-Benchmark GSM8K (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      Three-step GSM8K replication: (1) temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702 models,\n      (2) semi-synthetic injection validation, (3) GSM1K contamination gap correlation (N=33).\n    expected_results:\n      step1_temporal_c_pct: 18.9\n      step1_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n      step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n      step2_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.517\n      step3_pearson_r: -0.478\n      step3_pearson_p: 0.005\n      step3_spearman_rho: -0.403\n      step3_spearman_p: 0.020\n      step3_partial_r: -0.385\n      step3_partial_p: 0.027\n      step3_permutation_p: 0.014\n      step3_n_models: 33\n      step3_bca_ci_pearson: [-0.714, -0.155]\n      step3_bca_ci_spearman: [-0.687, -0.031]\n      step3_leave_one_out_r_range: [-0.537, -0.374]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下 A6 假设成立：GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark evidence。\n      所有 CI 排除零。方向是 NEGATIVE（opposite to naive contamination hypothesis），但 best 档下评审\n      接受论文的解读：DIF-C items 抵抗 contamination-based gains，contamination 产生的 surface-level\n      improvement 集中在 non-DIF items。宽 CI（Pearson upper bound |r|=0.155, Spearman upper bound\n      near zero）被视为 honest reporting 而非 weakness。Leave-one-out stability 和 partial r 控制\n      overall accuracy 加分。至少 2/3 评审认为 N=33 sufficient for \"suggestive\" claim，不要求\n      \"definitive\"。Cook's d 分析排除单一 outlier 驱动。这是 Claim 4 的第四层 sub-finding，\n      不是 standalone claim——评审评价时将其视为 complementary evidence，不对其 standalone significance 设高标准。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: GSM1K Contamination Gap Correlation\"\n        columns: [method, statistic, value, p_value, \"95%_BCa_CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Pearson, r, -0.478, 0.005, \"[-0.714, -0.155]\"]\n          - [Spearman, ρ, -0.403, 0.020, \"[-0.687, -0.031]\"]\n          - [Partial_r, r_partial, -0.385, 0.027, \"[-0.640, -0.058]\"]\n          - [Permutation, p_perm, \"N/A\", 0.014, \"N/A\"]\n      - name: \"Table 3: GSM8K Temporal DIF\"\n        columns: [metric, standard_MH, external_MH, sanity]\n        rows:\n          - [C_pct, 18.9, 47.4, 0.3]\n          - [N_ref, 1017, 1017, 3350]\n          - [N_foc, 804, 804, 3352]\n          - [ΔTPR_p10, 0.818, 0.517, \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Scatter plot of model-level GSM1K contamination gap vs DIF-C item accuracy gap. r=-0.478, regression line with BCa CI band. Deepseek-math-7b-rl labeled as Cook's d max.\"\n      - \"Fig S3: GSM8K dose-response curve (ΔTPR vs injection probability p) for standard and external MH variants.\"\n    analysis: >\n      In best tier, Step 3 is the key value-add: cross-benchmark evidence that DIF items resist\n      contamination-based gains. The negative direction is the surprise finding that elevates the\n      paper — it's not what a naive contamination-detection paper would predict, but perfectly\n      consistent with the characterization narrative. Step 1 (C%=18.9%) confirms temporal DIF\n      generalizes beyond MMLU. Step 2 (ΔTPR=0.818) confirms the semi-synthetic framework is\n      portable. Reviewers appreciate the multi-step validation chain. One reviewer may note the\n      wide CI and small N, but in best tier this is flagged as \"appropriately caveated.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Bifactor IRT Equating Pilot (KILLED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      Bifactor IRT (1 general + 57 subject-specific factors) equating pilot. Killed after\n      plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1%.\n    expected_results:\n      status: killed\n      kill_reason: \"plan_014 pre-check: within-subject C%=38.1% (>25%), proving temporal DIF penetrates subject level\"\n      bifactor_would_have_achieved: \"At best marginal FPR reduction from 31% to ~27%, insufficient to justify complexity\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，bifactor kill 是 methodological honesty 的正面信号。评审看到的叙事是：\n      \"We tried three structural improvements (matched ability, θ-conditioning, bifactor pre-check),\n      all failed to reduce baseline FPR → this is an empirical observation about the nature of\n      temporal DIF in LLM benchmarks, not a fixable methodological limitation.\" A2 假设成立：\n      评审将 98% |Lz|>2 + bifactor failure 解读为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象。Limitations 中用 1-2 段\n      坦承即可，指向 multidimensional IRT future work。评审赞赏 \"we tried it, it didn't work,\n      here's what that tells us\" 的研究诚实性。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Killed experiment. In best tier, the killing is itself evidence — it contributes to the\n      \"empirical observation of structural constraints\" narrative in §5 Discussion. No reviewer\n      penalizes a well-documented null result that motivates future work.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Item Generation Calibration (PLANNED — dropped)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"item_generation_calibration\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM generation with\n      construct constraints + student simulation calibration.\n    expected_results:\n      status: not_executed\n      reason: \"Depends on plan_005 (bifactor) which was killed. Item generation without equating framework has no anchor.\"\n      hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_prompt: 0.28\n      hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_simulation: 0.71\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下不需要这个实验。Paper 已从 \"regeneration\" 彻底 pivot 到 \"characterization\"。\n      Claim 3 是 semi-synthetic validation framework，不是 item replacement pipeline。\n      评审不会要求 item generation 因为 paper 不声称解决 benchmark repair 问题——它声称提供\n      diagnostic lens。即使存在 regeneration 结果也会放 appendix。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dependency killed. Not needed for any of the 4 current claims. Paper's scope control\n      explicitly excludes regeneration from main body.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Cumulative Bayesian DIF (PLANNED — appendix only)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across 4 simulated successive administrations.\n      Show power improvement from cumulative evidence.\n    expected_results:\n      single_admin_power_delta10: 0.42\n      cumulative_2admin_power: 0.58\n      cumulative_3admin_power: 0.71\n      cumulative_4admin_power: 0.79\n      bayes_factor_threshold: 3.0\n      fpr_cumulative: 0.038\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 simulation 层面展现 clean power improvement\n      (0.42→0.79 over 4 administrations)，验证 longitudinal monitoring 理论可行性。\n      但 paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"simulation-only, underdeveloped\"，放 appendix。\n      评审不对 appendix 材料严格评审。在 best 档下，有 1 位评审可能在 \"interesting future direction\"\n      中提到这个结果，但不会影响分数。A3 假设的 \"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事不依赖此实验。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S4: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power\"\n        columns: [n_administrations, power_delta10, power_delta14, FPR]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.42, 0.68, 0.041]\n          - [2, 0.58, 0.82, 0.039]\n          - [3, 0.71, 0.91, 0.037]\n          - [4, 0.79, 0.95, 0.038]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S4: Power accumulation curve across successive administrations for δ=1.0 and δ=1.4.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix-only. Clean simulation result but not load-bearing for any claim. Best tier\n      treats this as \"bonus content that signals the authors thought ahead\" without affecting\n      the acceptance decision.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Graceful Degradation Analysis (PLANNED — appendix only)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"graceful_degradation_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement (5%, 10%, 20%, 50%).\n      Define validity metrics, simulate degradation, establish theoretical bounds.\n    expected_results:\n      rho_at_5pct_replacement: 0.999\n      rho_at_10pct_replacement: 0.997\n      rho_at_20pct_replacement: 0.993\n      rho_at_50pct_replacement: 0.975\n      reliability_alpha_full: 0.962\n      reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced: 0.948\n      construct_coverage_loss_at_20pct: 0.03\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，graceful degradation 直接支持 \"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事：即使替换 50%\n      items，ρ=0.975 且 reliability 仅降 0.014。但 paper_framing.md 将其标记为 supplementary，\n      depends on plan_005+006 which were killed。在 best 档下，plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997（DIF removal）\n      已经提供了等价的 evidence——graceful degradation 是 plan_017 的理论扩展，非必需。\n      即使不执行，Claim 4 的 redundancy sub-finding (ρ≈0.997) 已经 cover 了这个角度。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dependency killed (plan_005/006). Effectively replaced by plan_017's empirical ρ≈0.997\n      result. In best tier, plan_017 alone is sufficient for the redundancy argument.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Item-Focused Trees (PLANNED — appendix only)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"item_focused_trees\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) treating model release date as continuous\n      covariate. Alternative to categorical cohort DIF.\n    expected_results:\n      ift_flagged_items_pct: 28.7\n      ift_mh_concordance_jaccard: 0.72\n      ift_unique_detections: 412\n      mh_unique_detections: 738\n      ift_mh_overlap: 3180\n      continuous_date_splitting_r2: 0.31\n      ift_avoids_arbitrary_cutoff: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，IFT 作为 robustness check 展现 moderate concordance with MH (Jaccard=0.72)。\n      28.7% flagged items 接近 MH 的 31.3%，确认 temporal instability 不是 arbitrary cohort split\n      的产物。IFT 特有检测 (412 items) 反映 continuous temporal trends 而非 abrupt regime changes。\n      paper_framing.md 标记为 appendix robustness check。评审可能 appreciate 但不影响分数。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S5: IFT vs MH Concordance\"\n        columns: [method, items_flagged, overlap_with_MH, unique_detections, Jaccard]\n        rows:\n          - [MH_DIF, 3918, 3180, 738, \"—\"]\n          - [IFT, 3592, 3180, 412, 0.72]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S5: Release-date splits from IFT for 6 example items, showing continuous DIF trajectories vs MH binary classification.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix robustness check. In best tier, confirms MH findings are not artifacts of the\n      2023/2024 binary split. Clean supplementary evidence.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Architecture-Stratified DIF (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"architecture_stratified_dif\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      DIF within decoder-only models only (99.98% of METABENCH MMLU). Report IRT fit diagnostics,\n      compare C% vs full population.\n    expected_results:\n      decoder_only_pct: 99.98\n      decoder_only_n: 5226\n      non_decoder_n: 1\n      c_pct_decoder_only: 31.3\n      c_pct_full: 31.3\n      jaccard_decoder_vs_full: 1.0\n      irt_fit_unchanged: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，这个实验的结论极为干净：METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 模型是 decoder-only，\n      排除 1 个 non-decoder 模型后 C% 完全不变 (Jaccard=1.0)。这彻底消除 \"architecture heterogeneity\n      causes spurious DIF\" 的 concern。评审看到 99.98% homogeneity 后不会再追问 architecture confound。\n      A2 假设强化：98% |Lz|>2 不是 architecture mixing 导致的，而是 MMLU 57-subject 多维性的固有属性。\n      这是 proactive defense 的典范——Dream worst-case 识别的 concern 在实际数据中根本不存在。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S6: Architecture Composition\"\n        columns: [architecture, N, pct, C_pct_within]\n        rows:\n          - [decoder_only, 5226, 99.98, 31.3]\n          - [non_decoder, 1, 0.02, \"N/A (excluded)\"]\n          - [full_population, 5227, 100, 31.3]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Decisive negative result that kills the architecture confound concern in one number.\n      In best tier, this appears in §4.1 as a single sentence: \"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98%\n      decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model changes nothing\n      (Jaccard=1.0).\" Reviewers appreciate the thoroughness of checking.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_011: Semi-Synthetic Contamination Validation (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      Inject known differential contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure\n      DIF detection power (TPR/FPR) under controlled ground truth at varying injection rates.\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n      temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.548\n      temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.834\n      temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.990\n      temporal_external_tpr_p10: 1.000\n      temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n      matching_variable_contamination_confirmed: true\n      standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: \"0.298→0.616\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，semi-synthetic injection 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5\n      证明 DIF 确实能检测 differential contamination（不只是 capability improvement）。\n      清晰的 dose-response curve (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0) 展现 power 随 contamination severity\n      单调递增。FPR=0.314 不变证明 injection 不 inflate false positives（用 external matching variant）。\n      Standard MH 的 FPR inflation (0.298→0.616) 暴露了 matching variable contamination 问题——\n      这 motivates plan_016 的 cross-subject matching solution。评审认可 \"inject into real matrices,\n      not simulated\" 的方法论选择。A4 假设部分成立：semi-synthetic framework 是 reusable infrastructure\n      contribution，2/3 评审视其为 non-obvious methodological innovation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Injection Results (External MH)\"\n        columns: [injection_rate_p, TPR, FPR, ΔTPR]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0_baseline, 0.326, 0.314, \"—\"]\n          - [0.3, 0.548, 0.314, +0.222]\n          - [0.5, 0.834, 0.314, +0.508]\n          - [0.7, 0.990, 0.314, +0.664]\n          - [1.0, 1.000, 0.314, +0.674]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Dose-response curve showing TPR vs injection probability p for external MH. Monotonic increase with plateau at p≥0.7. FPR line flat at 0.314.\"\n      - \"Fig S6: Comparison of standard MH (FPR inflates) vs external MH (FPR stable) under injection, demonstrating matching variable contamination effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Load-bearing evidence for Claim 3. In best tier, the dose-response monotonicity and\n      FPR stability are the two key properties reviewers care about. The matching variable\n      contamination discovery (standard MH FPR inflates) adds methodological depth — it's\n      the kind of finding that makes reviewers trust the authors understand their method deeply.\n      Cross-subject matching solution (plan_016 ΔFPR=0.000) completes the story.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_018: Threshold Sensitivity (DONE — from paper_framing.md metrics)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"threshold_sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      ETS threshold robustness: C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5}. BH FDR\n      correction at q=0.05. Random-split sanity check.\n    expected_results:\n      c_pct_threshold_1_0: 48.9\n      c_pct_threshold_1_5: 31.3\n      c_pct_threshold_2_0: 18.3\n      c_pct_threshold_2_5: 10.2\n      bh_fdr_items_removed: 3\n      bh_fdr_c_pct_after: 31.30\n      bh_impact_negligible: true\n      finding_above_15pct_at_standard_thresholds: true\n      finding_above_10pct_at_conservative: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，threshold sensitivity 是 Claim 1 最强的 robustness evidence 之一。C% 从 48.9%\n      (liberal) 到 10.2% (most conservative) 的 monotonic decline 展现 finding 的 gradient nature——\n      不是 binary threshold artifact。即使在最保守的 |Δ_MH|≥2.5 下仍有 10.2% (1,278 items) 展现\n      large DIF。BH FDR 只移除 3/3,918 items 证明 ETS 双重要求（effect size + significance）\n      提供了几乎完整的隐式多重检验保护。A3 假设成立：评审接受 \"finding is robust across standard\n      thresholds\" 的 framing。诚实地报告 2.5 threshold 低于 15% 加分——shows intellectual honesty。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Threshold Sensitivity Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"|Δ_MH|_threshold\", \"ETS_class\", C_pct, N_items, BH_impact]\n        rows:\n          - [\"≥1.0\", C, 48.9, 6109, \"0 removed\"]\n          - [\"≥1.5\", C, 31.3, 3918, \"3 removed (→31.30%)\"]\n          - [\"≥2.0\", \"extreme_C\", 18.3, 2288, \"0 removed\"]\n          - [\"≥2.5\", \"extreme_C\", 10.2, 1278, \"0 removed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2b: Bar chart of C% across 4 thresholds with BH-corrected overlay (nearly invisible reduction).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Essential robustness for Claim 1. In best tier, the clean monotonic gradient and BH\n      near-zero impact are exactly what reviewers want to see. This pre-empts concern #7\n      (ETS threshold uncalibrated) and concern #8 (multiple testing) simultaneously.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_019: Instability Decomposition (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"instability_decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_019\"\n    description: >\n      Decompose temporal DIF into domain capability improvement vs item-specific instability.\n      Subject-level ecological correlation vs item-level logistic model.\n    expected_results:\n      subject_level_rho: 0.307\n      subject_level_p: 0.02\n      item_level_pseudo_r2: 0.0007\n      domain_improvement_contribution_pp: 2.4\n      domain_improvement_contribution_pct: 7.6\n      model1_primary: true\n      model2_simpson_supplementary: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，plan_019 是对 \"38% could just mean models got better\" concern 的决定性回应。\n      Subject-level ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，但 item-level decomposition\n      展现 pseudo R²=0.0007——domain improvement 只解释 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%)。这证明\n      instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 capability improvement 的 proxy。\n      A5 假设成立（与 plan_023 联合）：difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 提供了 mechanistic story——\n      capability improvement concentrates on hard items，而 easy items 的 difficulty structure\n      erodes。评审接受 \"ecological correlation grossly overstates item-level relationship\" 的\n      statistical reasoning。Model 1 vs Model 2 区分（confounder vs mediator）展现 methodological\n      sophistication。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S7: Instability Decomposition\"\n        columns: [level, metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [subject_level, Spearman_ρ, 0.307, \"modest ecological correlation\"]\n          - [subject_level, p_value, 0.02, \"significant but weak\"]\n          - [item_level, pseudo_R², 0.0007, \"domain improvement explains <1% variance\"]\n          - [item_level, contribution_pp, 2.4, \"of 31.3% C%, only 2.4pp from domain improvement\"]\n          - [item_level, contribution_pct, 7.6, \"92.4% of instability is item-specific\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S7: Left: subject-level ρ=0.307 scatter. Right: item-level decomposition showing 92.4% item-specific vs 7.6% domain-explained.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Resolves anticipated concern #1 definitively. In best tier, the two-level analysis\n      (ecological vs item-level) is exactly the methodological sophistication reviewers expect.\n      The 7.6% figure becomes a key talking point: \"less than 8% of temporal instability can\n      be attributed to models getting better.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: Circularity Ablation (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"circularity_ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      Compare DIF removal disruption vs alternative item selection heuristics\n      (accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination, random). Test whether\n      DIF's ranking disruption result is tautological.\n    expected_results:\n      dif_removal_z: -9.5\n      accuracy_gap_removal_z: -157\n      high_variance_removal_z: -108\n      high_discrimination_removal_z: -16\n      random_removal_z: 0\n      dif_vs_accgap_ratio: \"16×_less_disruptive\"\n      dif_vs_disc_ratio: \"1.7×_less_disruptive\"\n      dif_accgap_item_overlap_pct: 62.6\n      dif_disc_jaccard: 0.12\n      dif_disc_overlap_pct: 22.1\n      dif_rho_2024: 0.9970\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，circularity ablation 是 Claim 4 中最精巧的分析。尽管 DIF 和 accuracy-gap selection\n      有 62.6% item overlap，MH 的 ability conditioning 使 DIF removal 的 disruption 小 16 倍\n      (z=-9.5 vs z=-157)。这证明 MH 不是在找 \"大 accuracy gap\" items——它在控制能力后隔离了\n      genuine differential functioning。DIF-discrimination overlap 仅 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) 证明\n      DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations\" 而非 \"good items\"。\n      评审 concern #11 (tautology) 被彻底 refuted。A3 假设强化：DIF removal 仍然比 random 显著\n      (z=-9.5)，但远小于 naive heuristics——这就是 \"DIF items carry signal but are NOT the most\n      ranking-defining items\" 的 precise meaning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Circularity Ablation (Ranking Disruption by Removal Strategy)\"\n        columns: [strategy, n_items, ρ_full_vs_subset, disruption_z, overlap_with_DIF_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [random_baseline, 3918, 0.9985, 0, \"—\"]\n          - [DIF_C_removal, 3918, 0.9970, -9.5, 100]\n          - [high_discrimination, 3918, 0.9958, -16, 22.1]\n          - [high_variance, 3918, 0.9831, -108, 41.3]\n          - [accuracy_gap, 3918, 0.9712, -157, 62.6]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Bar chart of disruption z-scores by removal strategy. DIF is closest to random despite 62.6% overlap with accuracy-gap. Demonstrates MH conditioning effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Key evidence for Claim 4 sub-finding 2. In best tier, this analysis demonstrates deep\n      methodological understanding. The 62.6% overlap + 16× disruption gap is the \"aha moment\"\n      that convinces reviewers MH-DIF is doing something genuinely different from naive accuracy\n      comparison. Tautology concern fully resolved.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021: Non-Uniform DIF Robustness (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"nonuniform_dif_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects (1,787 items). Test MH's uniform-only\n      assumption and quantify non-uniform DIF prevalence.\n    expected_results:\n      n_subjects: 9\n      n_items: 1787\n      mh_lr_concordance: 0.921\n      nonuniform_dif_significance_pct: 38.7\n      nonuniform_dif_effect_size_pct: 24.8\n      mh_conservative_estimate_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，LR-DIF 的 92.1% concordance with MH 证明 MH classification 对 uniform DIF\n      是 robust。38.7% non-uniform DIF at significance threshold, 24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5\n      证明 MH 结构性地 underestimates instability——31% 是 conservative estimate。\n      评审 concern #9 (only uniform DIF) 被直接回应：\"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative;\n      including non-uniform DIF raises it to ~25% additional items.\" Best 档下评审接受 caveat\n      (LR used within-subject matching vs MH's cross-benchmark) 并同意使用 24.8% (effect-size\n      controlled) 而非 38.7% (significance-only)。这展现方法论 conservatism。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S8: Non-Uniform DIF (Logistic Regression)\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [MH_LR_C_concordance, \"92.1%\"]\n          - [non_uniform_DIF_significance, \"38.7%\"]\n          - [non_uniform_DIF_effect_size, \"24.8% (|β_int|≥0.5)\"]\n          - [n_subjects_tested, 9]\n          - [n_items_tested, 1787]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S8: MH classification vs LR classification confusion matrix. 92.1% concordance for ETS C class.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix robustness check. In best tier, the key message is \"31% is conservative\" —\n      this flips a potential weakness (MH is old/simple) into a strength (our estimate is\n      a lower bound). The 24.8% effect-size-controlled figure is the one used in the paper text.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_022: Model Independence (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"model_independence\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}. Compare C% at\n      each cap vs random subsample of same size. Test whether family structure inflates DIF.\n    expected_results:\n      k20_n_models: 447\n      k20_c_pct: 29.1\n      k20_random_c_pct: 30.9\n      k10_c_pct: 24.3\n      k10_random_c_pct: 27.5\n      k5_n_models: 146\n      k5_c_pct: 11.7\n      k5_random_c_pct: 16.9\n      k1_n_models: 33\n      k1_c_pct: 0.17\n      k1_note: \"underpowered (N<80)\"\n      family_inflates_c_pct: false\n      dif_at_every_cap_leq_random: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，graduated de-duplication 是对 concern #10 (model non-independence) 的决定性回应。\n      在每个 cap K 下，family-capped C% ≤ random subsample C%。K=20: 29.1% vs 30.9%,\n      K=5: 11.7% vs 16.9%。Family structure 不仅不 inflate C%，反而 slightly reduces it。\n      K=1 (33 families) 的 0.17% 是 underpowered (N<80) 导致 MH test 无法达到 significance，\n      不是 DIF 消失。评审接受 graduated design 的 methodological rigor——不是 cherry-pick 一个 K，\n      而是 show monotonic trend。A1 假设强化：31.3% 是 genuine 的，not an artifact of model duplication。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S9: Model Independence — Graduated De-duplication\"\n        columns: [cap_K, N_models, C_pct_family_cap, C_pct_random_subsample, delta]\n        rows:\n          - [20, 447, 29.1, 30.9, -1.8]\n          - [10, 283, 24.3, 27.5, -3.2]\n          - [5, 146, 11.7, 16.9, -5.2]\n          - [2, 66, 2.1, 5.8, -3.7]\n          - [1, 33, 0.17, 0.84, \"-0.67 (underpowered)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S9: Paired line plot of C% (family-capped vs random subsample) at each K. Family-capped consistently at or below random.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Resolves concern #10. In best tier, the graduated design is elegant — it shows the\n      relationship between sample independence and DIF detection is not driven by model\n      family inflation. The \"family C% ≤ random C%\" pattern at every K is stronger than\n      just showing \"similar\" — it shows family structure, if anything, suppresses DIF detection.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Item Characterization (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"item_characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      Characterize DIF-C items by difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution, and\n      DIF direction. Key finding: difficulty×direction interaction.\n    expected_results:\n      difficulty_cohen_d: -0.247\n      discrimination_cohen_d: 0.230\n      domain_chi2_p: 0.32\n      domain_uniformly_distributed: true\n      direction_focal_favoring_pct: 43.9\n      direction_reference_favoring_pct: 56.1\n      difficulty_direction_rho: -0.597\n      hardest_decile_focal_favoring_pct: 88.7\n      easiest_decile_reference_favoring_pct: 96.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，plan_023 是 Claim 4 的 surprise finding 升华全文。difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597\n      揭示了一个系统性 pattern：hardest-decile DIF-C items 88.7% favor 2024 models（capability\n      improvement concentrates on hard items），easiest-decile 96.2% favor 2023 models（easy items'\n      difficulty structure erodes across generations）。这从纯粹描述性的 \"31% are unstable\" 升级为\n      mechanistic story：\"which items changed and in what direction tells us about the nature of\n      capability improvement.\" A5 假设成立：difficulty×direction 作为 'capability improvement\n      concentrates on hard items' 的 mechanistic story 引起评审共鸣。DIF-C items moderately harder\n      (d=-0.247) 和 higher discrimination (d=0.230) 是 sensible——functionally changing items 倾向于\n      是更有区分度的 items。Domain uniformity (χ² p=0.32) 证明 instability 不 cluster 在特定领域——\n      这是 cross-domain phenomenon，strengthening generalizability。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Item Characterization of DIF-C Items\"\n        columns: [property, DIF_C_mean, non_DIF_mean, Cohen_d, p_value]\n        rows:\n          - [difficulty_p, 0.58, 0.65, -0.247, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [discrimination_rpbis, 0.34, 0.28, 0.230, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [domain_distribution, \"uniform\", \"uniform\", \"χ²_p=0.32\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table 8: Difficulty × DIF Direction Interaction\"\n        columns: [difficulty_decile, n_DIF_C, pct_focal_favoring, pct_reference_favoring]\n        rows:\n          - [1_easiest, 287, 3.8, 96.2]\n          - [2, 312, 8.3, 91.7]\n          - [5_median, 401, 38.2, 61.8]\n          - [9, 478, 79.1, 20.9]\n          - [10_hardest, 512, 88.7, 11.3]\n          - [overall, 3918, 43.9, 56.1]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Stacked bar chart of DIF direction by difficulty decile. Clear gradient from 96.2% reference-favoring (easiest) to 88.7% focal-favoring (hardest). ρ=-0.597 annotation.\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Scatter plot of item difficulty vs Δ_MH, color-coded by direction. Strong negative trend visible.\"\n    analysis: >\n      The crown jewel of the paper in best tier. difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 transforms the\n      paper from \"we found instability\" to \"we understand what drives it.\" This is the finding\n      that makes reviewer #3 write \"interesting and novel\" in their review. The mechanistic\n      story (hard items improve, easy items erode) connects to the broader ML narrative about\n      capability scaling — it's the kind of finding that ML researchers can immediately relate to\n      their own experience with model training. Domain uniformity adds confidence that this is\n      a general phenomenon, not an artifact of specific knowledge domains.\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":639,"cache_read_input_tokens":54033,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":639},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff7feff5-12f0-4f3d-8a05-edb61f233b1a","uuid":"93eebf61-753a-45c0-8c70-c077bf15e7a8"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":394344,"duration_api_ms":395033,"num_turns":7,"result":"Now I have all the information needed. Let me compile the comprehensive best-tier predictions for all planned experiments.\n\n```yaml\ntier: best\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  全部四条 Claim 以完整力度着陆。\"31% of MMLU Items Are Functionally Unstable\" 作为 discovery paper\n  被接受。评审认可 \"old psychometric method × unprecedented LLM benchmark scale = genuine empirical discovery\"\n  的 novelty 逻辑。IRT misspecification（98% |Lz|>2）被视为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象，作为 honest limitation 处理，\n  指向 multidimensional IRT future work。\"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事清晰，ρ≈0.997 是 strength\n  （massive redundancy），31% 是 diagnostic signal。difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 作为 mechanistic story\n  引起共鸣。GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark evidence，宽 CI 被接受为 honest reporting。\n  reviewer_avg_score: 6.5, acceptance_probability_pct: 68, claims_at_full_strength: 4,\n  novelty_sub_score_avg: 3.0, reviewers_flagging_irt_as_fatal: 0, major_revisions_needed: 0-1。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_001: Real Data DIF on MMLU (DONE — predict best-tier interpretation)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"real_data_dif_mmlu\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_001\"\n    description: >\n      MH-DIF applied to METABENCH MMLU response matrix (5,227 models × 12,508 items).\n      Temporal cohort (2023 vs 2024-H1), ability-quintile cohort, within-family confound control,\n      domain-specificity analysis, random-split sanity check.\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_ets_c_pct: 31.3\n      temporal_fpr_li_clean: 0.318\n      temporal_enrichment: 0.96\n      ability_ets_c_pct: 2.9\n      ability_enrichment: 1.19\n      within_family_llama2v3_c_pct: 61.3\n      domain_spearman_rho: 0.307\n      domain_spearman_p: 0.02\n      sanity_random_split_c_pct: 0.18\n      temporal_ability_jaccard: 0.014\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，31.3% temporal C% 被评审接受为 genuine empirical discovery——这是首次对 LLM benchmark\n      做如此大规模的 DIF 分析。enrichment≈0.96 不再被解读为 \"DIF 失败\"，而是完美支撑 Claim 2 的 meta-critique：\n      Li et al. web-overlap labels 测量的是 global exposure，不是 differential contamination，因此\n      enrichment≈1.0 是 expected。random split 0.18% 彻底排除统计伪像。domain ρ=0.307 是 modest\n      ecological correlation，但 plan_019 的 item-level decomposition（≤2.4pp/7.6%）证明 instability\n      是 predominantly item-specific，不是 \"models got better\" 的 proxy。评审认可这组结果的 completeness\n      和 methodological rigor（4-way sensitivity matrix + sanity checks）。A1 假设成立：ML 评审接受\n      \"established psychometric method at unprecedented scale\" 的 novelty 逻辑。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 1: Temporal DIF Summary\"\n        columns: [cohort_definition, N_ref, N_foc, ETS_A_pct, ETS_B_pct, ETS_C_pct, enrichment_vs_Li]\n        rows:\n          - [temporal_2023v2024, 1253, 656, 45.2, 23.5, 31.3, 0.96]\n          - [ability_quintile, 2613, 2614, 90.8, 6.3, 2.9, 1.19]\n          - [random_split_sanity, 2613, 2614, 99.6, 0.2, 0.18, \"N/A\"]\n      - name: \"Table 2: Domain-Specificity (57 subjects)\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [C%_range, \"20.7–48.4%\"]\n          - [unweighted_mean, \"~30%\"]\n          - [ρ_vs_accuracy_improvement, 0.307]\n          - [p_value, 0.02]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 1: Heatmap of 57-subject C% sorted by domain cluster. All subjects show >20% C%. Color gradient from green (20%) to red (48%).\"\n      - \"Fig 2: Scatter plot of subject-level C% vs accuracy improvement (ρ=0.307). Modest positive trend, large residual variance emphasizes item-specific drivers.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_001 provides the headline finding. In best tier, the pivot from \"contamination detector\"\n      to \"benchmark characterization\" is complete and compelling. The 31.3% figure survives all\n      robustness checks (plans 018, 019, 020, 022). Within-family Llama-2v3 C%=61.3% is reframed\n      as evidence of genuine capability evolution, not a confound. Two reviewers note the thoroughness\n      of the multi-cohort design; one asks about non-uniform DIF (addressed by plan_021).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_002: RL Robustness Validation (PLANNED — not in registry)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"rl_robustness_validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_002\"\n    description: >\n      Validate DIF robustness to RL training: SFT-only baseline, alignment-RL (DPO/ORPO, N=477),\n      10-15 reasoning-RL models (GRPO/PPO) added to focal cohort. Compare DIF retention vs\n      traditional detector (Min-K%, ConStat) degradation on RL models.\n    expected_results:\n      sft_baseline_c_pct: 30.8\n      alignment_rl_cohort_c_pct: 31.1\n      reasoning_rl_mixed_cohort_c_pct: 30.5\n      jaccard_sft_vs_alignment_rl: 0.89\n      jaccard_sft_vs_reasoning_rl_mixed: 0.86\n      dif_retention_ratio: 0.97\n      constat_auroc_sft: 0.72\n      constat_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.41\n      mink_auroc_sft: 0.68\n      mink_auroc_reasoning_rl: 0.35\n      tost_equivalence_p: 0.008\n      bootstrap_ci_dif_retention: [0.93, 1.01]\n      n_reasoning_rl_models: 13\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，DIF 的 group-level 设计天然免疫 RL。MH-DIF 在 matched-score strata 内比较 item\n      通过率——它不依赖单个模型的 NLL 分布（Min-K%）或 perturbation 响应（ConStat），因此 RL 训练后的 NLL gap\n      contraction 和 generation distribution 变化不影响 DIF。A1 假设成立：评审理解 DIF 是 group-level\n      统计量，13 个 RL 模型混入 ~800+ focal cohort 不会改变 strata 构成。SFT vs alignment-RL Jaccard=0.89\n      反映 DPO/ORPO 不改变 item functioning。ConStat/Min-K% AUROC 从 0.68-0.72 降至 0.35-0.41 提供了\n      explicit contrast。TOST 等价性检验 p=0.008 正式确认 DIF retention。但评审可能注意到 N=13 reasoning-RL\n      太少，最多 1 位评审要求更多模型——在 best 档下这被视为 minor concern 而非 fatal。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S1: DIF Robustness to Training Paradigm\"\n        columns: [cohort_composition, N_total, C_pct, Jaccard_vs_SFT, retention_ratio]\n        rows:\n          - [SFT_only, 380, 30.8, 1.00, 1.00]\n          - [alignment_RL_DPO_ORPO, 477, 31.1, 0.89, 0.97]\n          - [mixed_reasoning_RL, 393, 30.5, 0.86, 0.97]\n      - name: \"Table S2: Traditional Detector Degradation\"\n        columns: [detector, AUROC_SFT, AUROC_reasoning_RL, delta, DeLong_p]\n        rows:\n          - [Min-K%, 0.68, 0.35, -0.33, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [ConStat, 0.72, 0.41, -0.31, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [DIF_MH, 0.93, 0.91, -0.02, 0.42]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S1: ROC curves for DIF vs Min-K% vs ConStat on SFT cohort (left) and reasoning-RL-mixed cohort (right). DIF curves nearly identical; traditional detectors collapse.\"\n    analysis: >\n      In best tier, this experiment lands as appendix-strength supporting evidence. The N=13\n      reasoning-RL limitation is acknowledged transparently. The key result is the contrast:\n      traditional detectors degrade dramatically while DIF is invariant. One reviewer may ask\n      whether DIF would still be robust if the focal cohort were majority RL — acknowledged as\n      future work given current reasoning-RL model scarcity. This experiment is NOT in the main\n      body (paper_framing.md already notes N=13 is underpowered → limitations disclosure, not claim).\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003a: ConStat Perturbation Evaluation (PLANNED — dropped from paper)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"constat_perturbation_eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003a\"\n    description: >\n      Independent ConStat-style perturbation testing on 200+ MMLU items. Generate paraphrases,\n      compare original vs reformulated performance, apply FDR-controlled detection.\n    expected_results:\n      n_items_paraphrased: 250\n      n_models_tested: 15\n      constat_detection_rate_sft: 0.34\n      constat_detection_rate_rl: 0.08\n      fdr_controlled_detections: 62\n      semantic_equivalence_score: 0.91\n      constat_fpr_on_clean: 0.06\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，ConStat 在非 RL 模型上展现 moderate detection power（~34%），但在 RL 模型上接近 chance\n      level（~8%），验证了 perturbation-based 方法对 RL 的脆弱性。这为 Claim 2 meta-critique 提供了\n      complementary baseline：ConStat 检测的是 verbatim memorization（对 paraphrase 敏感），而非\n      differential contamination。但 paper_framing.md 已将 plan_003a/b/c 标记为 \"never executed, future work\"，\n      所以即使结果干净，它只出现在 appendix 或 discussion 中作为 \"related method comparison\"。评审不要求\n      这个实验存在——paper 已经 pivoted 到 characterization narrative，不需要 detection method 比较。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S3: ConStat Baseline Performance\"\n        columns: [model_type, N_models, detection_rate, FDR_controlled_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [SFT, 8, 0.34, 27.2]\n          - [DPO/ORPO, 5, 0.21, 14.8]\n          - [reasoning_RL, 2, 0.08, 3.2]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S2: Detection rate by model training paradigm showing ConStat degradation under RL.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Dropped from main paper. In best tier, this would have been a clean baseline comparison but\n      is unnecessary for the characterization narrative. If executed, it strengthens the meta-critique\n      (Claim 2) by showing ConStat also can't distinguish web-overlap from differential contamination.\n      Paper framing correctly categorizes this as future work.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003b: DVD Generation Variance Evaluation (PLANNED — dropped from paper)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"dvd_generation_variance_eval\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003b\"\n    description: >\n      DVD generation variance on MMLU: 10-15 open-weight models, 50 responses per item via\n      temperature sampling, bimodal distribution detection for contamination.\n    expected_results:\n      n_models: 12\n      n_items_tested: 500\n      bimodal_items_detected: 47\n      dvd_auroc_vs_li_labels: 0.58\n      dvd_auroc_vs_semi_synthetic: 0.63\n      variant_contamination_sensitivity: 0.22\n      verbatim_contamination_sensitivity: 0.51\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，DVD 展现 moderate verbatim contamination sensitivity（0.51）但 variant contamination\n      几乎无效（0.22）。这是 DVD 方法的 known limitation——generation variance 需要 exact memorization\n      才能产生 bimodal 分布，variant contamination 只改变 posterior probability 不产生 bimodality。\n      与 plan_003a 一样，paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"never executed, future work\"。\n      在 best 档下评审不会因为缺少这个实验而扣分——paper 不声称做 detection method 比较。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dropped from main paper. Would have provided variant-contamination detection baseline.\n      Paper narrative has pivoted away from detection → characterization, making this unnecessary\n      for acceptance. Best tier does not require execution.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_003c: Ensemble Fusion (PLANNED — dropped from paper)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"ensemble_fusion\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_003c\"\n    description: >\n      Fuse DIF + ConStat + DVD into multi-signal ensemble with calibrated thresholds,\n      majority voting, weighted fusion, and cross-validated weights.\n    expected_results:\n      ensemble_tpr_at_fpr010: 0.78\n      ensemble_coverage_complementarity: 0.89\n      dif_unique_detections_pct: 31\n      constat_unique_detections_pct: 18\n      dvd_unique_detections_pct: 7\n      overlap_all_three_pct: 12\n      fusion_auroc: 0.82\n      uniform_weight_auroc: 0.79\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，三信号 ensemble 理论上能覆盖更多 contamination 类型（DIF: differential, ConStat: verbatim,\n      DVD: bimodal），但 paper_framing.md 明确将其标记为 \"never executed, future work\"。\n      Paper 已从 \"detection ensemble\" 彻底转向 \"characterization + meta-critique\"。\n      评审不会因为没有 ensemble 而降分——paper 的 novelty 来自 scale + meta-critique + framework，不是更好的检测器。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Explicitly dropped. Not needed for best-tier acceptance under the current characterization\n      framing. Would only matter if the paper claimed to build a better contamination detector,\n      which it does not.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_004: Cross-Benchmark GSM8K (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"cross_benchmark_gsm8k\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_004\"\n    description: >\n      Three-step GSM8K replication: (1) temporal DIF on 1,319 items × 6,702 models,\n      (2) semi-synthetic injection validation, (3) GSM1K contamination gap correlation (N=33).\n    expected_results:\n      step1_temporal_c_pct: 18.9\n      step1_sanity_c_pct: 0.3\n      step2_standard_delta_tpr_p10: 0.818\n      step2_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.517\n      step3_pearson_r: -0.478\n      step3_pearson_p: 0.005\n      step3_spearman_rho: -0.403\n      step3_spearman_p: 0.020\n      step3_partial_r: -0.385\n      step3_partial_p: 0.027\n      step3_permutation_p: 0.014\n      step3_n_models: 33\n      step3_bca_ci_pearson: [-0.714, -0.155]\n      step3_bca_ci_spearman: [-0.687, -0.031]\n      step3_leave_one_out_r_range: [-0.537, -0.374]\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下 A6 假设成立：GSM1K r=-0.478 (N=33) 被视为 suggestive cross-benchmark evidence。\n      所有 CI 排除零。方向是 NEGATIVE（opposite to naive contamination hypothesis），但 best 档下评审\n      接受论文的解读：DIF-C items 抵抗 contamination-based gains，contamination 产生的 surface-level\n      improvement 集中在 non-DIF items。宽 CI（Pearson upper bound |r|=0.155, Spearman upper bound\n      near zero）被视为 honest reporting 而非 weakness。Leave-one-out stability 和 partial r 控制\n      overall accuracy 加分。至少 2/3 评审认为 N=33 sufficient for \"suggestive\" claim，不要求\n      \"definitive\"。Cook's d 分析排除单一 outlier 驱动。这是 Claim 4 的第四层 sub-finding，\n      不是 standalone claim——评审评价时将其视为 complementary evidence，不对其 standalone significance 设高标准。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: GSM1K Contamination Gap Correlation\"\n        columns: [method, statistic, value, p_value, \"95%_BCa_CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [Pearson, r, -0.478, 0.005, \"[-0.714, -0.155]\"]\n          - [Spearman, ρ, -0.403, 0.020, \"[-0.687, -0.031]\"]\n          - [Partial_r, r_partial, -0.385, 0.027, \"[-0.640, -0.058]\"]\n          - [Permutation, p_perm, \"N/A\", 0.014, \"N/A\"]\n      - name: \"Table 3: GSM8K Temporal DIF\"\n        columns: [metric, standard_MH, external_MH, sanity]\n        rows:\n          - [C_pct, 18.9, 47.4, 0.3]\n          - [N_ref, 1017, 1017, 3350]\n          - [N_foc, 804, 804, 3352]\n          - [ΔTPR_p10, 0.818, 0.517, \"N/A\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 4: Scatter plot of model-level GSM1K contamination gap vs DIF-C item accuracy gap. r=-0.478, regression line with BCa CI band. Deepseek-math-7b-rl labeled as Cook's d max.\"\n      - \"Fig S3: GSM8K dose-response curve (ΔTPR vs injection probability p) for standard and external MH variants.\"\n    analysis: >\n      In best tier, Step 3 is the key value-add: cross-benchmark evidence that DIF items resist\n      contamination-based gains. The negative direction is the surprise finding that elevates the\n      paper — it's not what a naive contamination-detection paper would predict, but perfectly\n      consistent with the characterization narrative. Step 1 (C%=18.9%) confirms temporal DIF\n      generalizes beyond MMLU. Step 2 (ΔTPR=0.818) confirms the semi-synthetic framework is\n      portable. Reviewers appreciate the multi-step validation chain. One reviewer may note the\n      wide CI and small N, but in best tier this is flagged as \"appropriately caveated.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_005: Bifactor IRT Equating Pilot (KILLED)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"bifactor_irt_equating_pilot\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_005\"\n    description: >\n      Bifactor IRT (1 general + 57 subject-specific factors) equating pilot. Killed after\n      plan_014 pre-check showed within-subject C%=38.1%.\n    expected_results:\n      status: killed\n      kill_reason: \"plan_014 pre-check: within-subject C%=38.1% (>25%), proving temporal DIF penetrates subject level\"\n      bifactor_would_have_achieved: \"At best marginal FPR reduction from 31% to ~27%, insufficient to justify complexity\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，bifactor kill 是 methodological honesty 的正面信号。评审看到的叙事是：\n      \"We tried three structural improvements (matched ability, θ-conditioning, bifactor pre-check),\n      all failed to reduce baseline FPR → this is an empirical observation about the nature of\n      temporal DIF in LLM benchmarks, not a fixable methodological limitation.\" A2 假设成立：\n      评审将 98% |Lz|>2 + bifactor failure 解读为 MMLU 固有多维性的已知现象。Limitations 中用 1-2 段\n      坦承即可，指向 multidimensional IRT future work。评审赞赏 \"we tried it, it didn't work,\n      here's what that tells us\" 的研究诚实性。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Killed experiment. In best tier, the killing is itself evidence — it contributes to the\n      \"empirical observation of structural constraints\" narrative in §5 Discussion. No reviewer\n      penalizes a well-documented null result that motivates future work.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_006: Item Generation Calibration (PLANNED — dropped)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"item_generation_calibration\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_006\"\n    description: >\n      Generate replacement items for DIF-flagged MMLU questions via LLM generation with\n      construct constraints + student simulation calibration.\n    expected_results:\n      status: not_executed\n      reason: \"Depends on plan_005 (bifactor) which was killed. Item generation without equating framework has no anchor.\"\n      hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_prompt: 0.28\n      hypothetical_difficulty_correlation_simulation: 0.71\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下不需要这个实验。Paper 已从 \"regeneration\" 彻底 pivot 到 \"characterization\"。\n      Claim 3 是 semi-synthetic validation framework，不是 item replacement pipeline。\n      评审不会要求 item generation 因为 paper 不声称解决 benchmark repair 问题——它声称提供\n      diagnostic lens。即使存在 regeneration 结果也会放 appendix。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dependency killed. Not needed for any of the 4 current claims. Paper's scope control\n      explicitly excludes regeneration from main body.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_007: Cumulative Bayesian DIF (PLANNED — appendix only)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"cumulative_bayesian_dif\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_007\"\n    description: >\n      Bayesian DIF priors (Sinharay et al., 2006) across 4 simulated successive administrations.\n      Show power improvement from cumulative evidence.\n    expected_results:\n      single_admin_power_delta10: 0.42\n      cumulative_2admin_power: 0.58\n      cumulative_3admin_power: 0.71\n      cumulative_4admin_power: 0.79\n      bayes_factor_threshold: 3.0\n      fpr_cumulative: 0.038\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，cumulative Bayesian DIF 在 simulation 层面展现 clean power improvement\n      (0.42→0.79 over 4 administrations)，验证 longitudinal monitoring 理论可行性。\n      但 paper_framing.md 已将其标记为 \"simulation-only, underdeveloped\"，放 appendix。\n      评审不对 appendix 材料严格评审。在 best 档下，有 1 位评审可能在 \"interesting future direction\"\n      中提到这个结果，但不会影响分数。A3 假设的 \"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事不依赖此实验。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S4: Cumulative Bayesian DIF Power\"\n        columns: [n_administrations, power_delta10, power_delta14, FPR]\n        rows:\n          - [1, 0.42, 0.68, 0.041]\n          - [2, 0.58, 0.82, 0.039]\n          - [3, 0.71, 0.91, 0.037]\n          - [4, 0.79, 0.95, 0.038]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S4: Power accumulation curve across successive administrations for δ=1.0 and δ=1.4.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix-only. Clean simulation result but not load-bearing for any claim. Best tier\n      treats this as \"bonus content that signals the authors thought ahead\" without affecting\n      the acceptance decision.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_008: Graceful Degradation Analysis (PLANNED — appendix only)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"graceful_degradation_analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_008\"\n    description: >\n      Formal analysis of benchmark validity under progressive item replacement (5%, 10%, 20%, 50%).\n      Define validity metrics, simulate degradation, establish theoretical bounds.\n    expected_results:\n      rho_at_5pct_replacement: 0.999\n      rho_at_10pct_replacement: 0.997\n      rho_at_20pct_replacement: 0.993\n      rho_at_50pct_replacement: 0.975\n      reliability_alpha_full: 0.962\n      reliability_alpha_50pct_replaced: 0.948\n      construct_coverage_loss_at_20pct: 0.03\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，graceful degradation 直接支持 \"instability ≠ invalidity\" 叙事：即使替换 50%\n      items，ρ=0.975 且 reliability 仅降 0.014。但 paper_framing.md 将其标记为 supplementary，\n      depends on plan_005+006 which were killed。在 best 档下，plan_017 的 ρ≈0.997（DIF removal）\n      已经提供了等价的 evidence——graceful degradation 是 plan_017 的理论扩展，非必需。\n      即使不执行，Claim 4 的 redundancy sub-finding (ρ≈0.997) 已经 cover 了这个角度。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Dependency killed (plan_005/006). Effectively replaced by plan_017's empirical ρ≈0.997\n      result. In best tier, plan_017 alone is sufficient for the redundancy argument.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_009: Item-Focused Trees (PLANNED — appendix only)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"item_focused_trees\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_009\"\n    description: >\n      Item-Focused Trees (Tutz & Berger, 2016) treating model release date as continuous\n      covariate. Alternative to categorical cohort DIF.\n    expected_results:\n      ift_flagged_items_pct: 28.7\n      ift_mh_concordance_jaccard: 0.72\n      ift_unique_detections: 412\n      mh_unique_detections: 738\n      ift_mh_overlap: 3180\n      continuous_date_splitting_r2: 0.31\n      ift_avoids_arbitrary_cutoff: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，IFT 作为 robustness check 展现 moderate concordance with MH (Jaccard=0.72)。\n      28.7% flagged items 接近 MH 的 31.3%，确认 temporal instability 不是 arbitrary cohort split\n      的产物。IFT 特有检测 (412 items) 反映 continuous temporal trends 而非 abrupt regime changes。\n      paper_framing.md 标记为 appendix robustness check。评审可能 appreciate 但不影响分数。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S5: IFT vs MH Concordance\"\n        columns: [method, items_flagged, overlap_with_MH, unique_detections, Jaccard]\n        rows:\n          - [MH_DIF, 3918, 3180, 738, \"—\"]\n          - [IFT, 3592, 3180, 412, 0.72]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S5: Release-date splits from IFT for 6 example items, showing continuous DIF trajectories vs MH binary classification.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix robustness check. In best tier, confirms MH findings are not artifacts of the\n      2023/2024 binary split. Clean supplementary evidence.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_010: Architecture-Stratified DIF (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"architecture_stratified_dif\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_010\"\n    description: >\n      DIF within decoder-only models only (99.98% of METABENCH MMLU). Report IRT fit diagnostics,\n      compare C% vs full population.\n    expected_results:\n      decoder_only_pct: 99.98\n      decoder_only_n: 5226\n      non_decoder_n: 1\n      c_pct_decoder_only: 31.3\n      c_pct_full: 31.3\n      jaccard_decoder_vs_full: 1.0\n      irt_fit_unchanged: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，这个实验的结论极为干净：METABENCH MMLU 中 5226/5227 模型是 decoder-only，\n      排除 1 个 non-decoder 模型后 C% 完全不变 (Jaccard=1.0)。这彻底消除 \"architecture heterogeneity\n      causes spurious DIF\" 的 concern。评审看到 99.98% homogeneity 后不会再追问 architecture confound。\n      A2 假设强化：98% |Lz|>2 不是 architecture mixing 导致的，而是 MMLU 57-subject 多维性的固有属性。\n      这是 proactive defense 的典范——Dream worst-case 识别的 concern 在实际数据中根本不存在。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S6: Architecture Composition\"\n        columns: [architecture, N, pct, C_pct_within]\n        rows:\n          - [decoder_only, 5226, 99.98, 31.3]\n          - [non_decoder, 1, 0.02, \"N/A (excluded)\"]\n          - [full_population, 5227, 100, 31.3]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Decisive negative result that kills the architecture confound concern in one number.\n      In best tier, this appears in §4.1 as a single sentence: \"METABENCH MMLU is 99.98%\n      decoder-only (5,226/5,227); excluding the single non-decoder model changes nothing\n      (Jaccard=1.0).\" Reviewers appreciate the thoroughness of checking.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_011: Semi-Synthetic Contamination Validation (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"semi_synthetic_contamination_validation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_011\"\n    description: >\n      Inject known differential contamination into real METABENCH response matrix. Measure\n      DIF detection power (TPR/FPR) under controlled ground truth at varying injection rates.\n    expected_results:\n      temporal_external_tpr_p0: 0.326\n      temporal_external_tpr_p03: 0.548\n      temporal_external_tpr_p05: 0.834\n      temporal_external_tpr_p07: 0.990\n      temporal_external_tpr_p10: 1.000\n      temporal_external_fpr: 0.314\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p05: 0.508\n      temporal_external_delta_tpr_p10: 0.674\n      dose_response_monotonic: true\n      matching_variable_contamination_confirmed: true\n      standard_mh_fpr_inflation_at_p10: \"0.298→0.616\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，semi-synthetic injection 是 Claim 3 的核心 evidence。ΔTPR=+0.508 at p=0.5\n      证明 DIF 确实能检测 differential contamination（不只是 capability improvement）。\n      清晰的 dose-response curve (p=0.3→0.5→0.7→1.0) 展现 power 随 contamination severity\n      单调递增。FPR=0.314 不变证明 injection 不 inflate false positives（用 external matching variant）。\n      Standard MH 的 FPR inflation (0.298→0.616) 暴露了 matching variable contamination 问题——\n      这 motivates plan_016 的 cross-subject matching solution。评审认可 \"inject into real matrices,\n      not simulated\" 的方法论选择。A4 假设部分成立：semi-synthetic framework 是 reusable infrastructure\n      contribution，2/3 评审视其为 non-obvious methodological innovation。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Semi-Synthetic Injection Results (External MH)\"\n        columns: [injection_rate_p, TPR, FPR, ΔTPR]\n        rows:\n          - [0.0_baseline, 0.326, 0.314, \"—\"]\n          - [0.3, 0.548, 0.314, +0.222]\n          - [0.5, 0.834, 0.314, +0.508]\n          - [0.7, 0.990, 0.314, +0.664]\n          - [1.0, 1.000, 0.314, +0.674]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 3: Dose-response curve showing TPR vs injection probability p for external MH. Monotonic increase with plateau at p≥0.7. FPR line flat at 0.314.\"\n      - \"Fig S6: Comparison of standard MH (FPR inflates) vs external MH (FPR stable) under injection, demonstrating matching variable contamination effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Load-bearing evidence for Claim 3. In best tier, the dose-response monotonicity and\n      FPR stability are the two key properties reviewers care about. The matching variable\n      contamination discovery (standard MH FPR inflates) adds methodological depth — it's\n      the kind of finding that makes reviewers trust the authors understand their method deeply.\n      Cross-subject matching solution (plan_016 ΔFPR=0.000) completes the story.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_018: Threshold Sensitivity (DONE — from paper_framing.md metrics)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"threshold_sensitivity\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_018\"\n    description: >\n      ETS threshold robustness: C% at |Δ_MH| thresholds {1.0, 1.5, 2.0, 2.5}. BH FDR\n      correction at q=0.05. Random-split sanity check.\n    expected_results:\n      c_pct_threshold_1_0: 48.9\n      c_pct_threshold_1_5: 31.3\n      c_pct_threshold_2_0: 18.3\n      c_pct_threshold_2_5: 10.2\n      bh_fdr_items_removed: 3\n      bh_fdr_c_pct_after: 31.30\n      bh_impact_negligible: true\n      finding_above_15pct_at_standard_thresholds: true\n      finding_above_10pct_at_conservative: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，threshold sensitivity 是 Claim 1 最强的 robustness evidence 之一。C% 从 48.9%\n      (liberal) 到 10.2% (most conservative) 的 monotonic decline 展现 finding 的 gradient nature——\n      不是 binary threshold artifact。即使在最保守的 |Δ_MH|≥2.5 下仍有 10.2% (1,278 items) 展现\n      large DIF。BH FDR 只移除 3/3,918 items 证明 ETS 双重要求（effect size + significance）\n      提供了几乎完整的隐式多重检验保护。A3 假设成立：评审接受 \"finding is robust across standard\n      thresholds\" 的 framing。诚实地报告 2.5 threshold 低于 15% 加分——shows intellectual honesty。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Threshold Sensitivity Analysis\"\n        columns: [\"|Δ_MH|_threshold\", \"ETS_class\", C_pct, N_items, BH_impact]\n        rows:\n          - [\"≥1.0\", C, 48.9, 6109, \"0 removed\"]\n          - [\"≥1.5\", C, 31.3, 3918, \"3 removed (→31.30%)\"]\n          - [\"≥2.0\", \"extreme_C\", 18.3, 2288, \"0 removed\"]\n          - [\"≥2.5\", \"extreme_C\", 10.2, 1278, \"0 removed\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 2b: Bar chart of C% across 4 thresholds with BH-corrected overlay (nearly invisible reduction).\"\n    analysis: >\n      Essential robustness for Claim 1. In best tier, the clean monotonic gradient and BH\n      near-zero impact are exactly what reviewers want to see. This pre-empts concern #7\n      (ETS threshold uncalibrated) and concern #8 (multiple testing) simultaneously.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_019: Instability Decomposition (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"instability_decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_019\"\n    description: >\n      Decompose temporal DIF into domain capability improvement vs item-specific instability.\n      Subject-level ecological correlation vs item-level logistic model.\n    expected_results:\n      subject_level_rho: 0.307\n      subject_level_p: 0.02\n      item_level_pseudo_r2: 0.0007\n      domain_improvement_contribution_pp: 2.4\n      domain_improvement_contribution_pct: 7.6\n      model1_primary: true\n      model2_simpson_supplementary: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，plan_019 是对 \"38% could just mean models got better\" concern 的决定性回应。\n      Subject-level ρ=0.307 (p=0.02) 是 modest ecological correlation，但 item-level decomposition\n      展现 pseudo R²=0.0007——domain improvement 只解释 2.4pp of 31.3% C% (7.6%)。这证明\n      instability 是 predominantly item-specific，不是 capability improvement 的 proxy。\n      A5 假设成立（与 plan_023 联合）：difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 提供了 mechanistic story——\n      capability improvement concentrates on hard items，而 easy items 的 difficulty structure\n      erodes。评审接受 \"ecological correlation grossly overstates item-level relationship\" 的\n      statistical reasoning。Model 1 vs Model 2 区分（confounder vs mediator）展现 methodological\n      sophistication。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S7: Instability Decomposition\"\n        columns: [level, metric, value, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [subject_level, Spearman_ρ, 0.307, \"modest ecological correlation\"]\n          - [subject_level, p_value, 0.02, \"significant but weak\"]\n          - [item_level, pseudo_R², 0.0007, \"domain improvement explains <1% variance\"]\n          - [item_level, contribution_pp, 2.4, \"of 31.3% C%, only 2.4pp from domain improvement\"]\n          - [item_level, contribution_pct, 7.6, \"92.4% of instability is item-specific\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S7: Left: subject-level ρ=0.307 scatter. Right: item-level decomposition showing 92.4% item-specific vs 7.6% domain-explained.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Resolves anticipated concern #1 definitively. In best tier, the two-level analysis\n      (ecological vs item-level) is exactly the methodological sophistication reviewers expect.\n      The 7.6% figure becomes a key talking point: \"less than 8% of temporal instability can\n      be attributed to models getting better.\"\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_020: Circularity Ablation (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"circularity_ablation\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_020\"\n    description: >\n      Compare DIF removal disruption vs alternative item selection heuristics\n      (accuracy-gap, high-variance, high-discrimination, random). Test whether\n      DIF's ranking disruption result is tautological.\n    expected_results:\n      dif_removal_z: -9.5\n      accuracy_gap_removal_z: -157\n      high_variance_removal_z: -108\n      high_discrimination_removal_z: -16\n      random_removal_z: 0\n      dif_vs_accgap_ratio: \"16×_less_disruptive\"\n      dif_vs_disc_ratio: \"1.7×_less_disruptive\"\n      dif_accgap_item_overlap_pct: 62.6\n      dif_disc_jaccard: 0.12\n      dif_disc_overlap_pct: 22.1\n      dif_rho_2024: 0.9970\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，circularity ablation 是 Claim 4 中最精巧的分析。尽管 DIF 和 accuracy-gap selection\n      有 62.6% item overlap，MH 的 ability conditioning 使 DIF removal 的 disruption 小 16 倍\n      (z=-9.5 vs z=-157)。这证明 MH 不是在找 \"大 accuracy gap\" items——它在控制能力后隔离了\n      genuine differential functioning。DIF-discrimination overlap 仅 22.1% (Jaccard=0.12) 证明\n      DIF identifies \"items that changed across generations\" 而非 \"good items\"。\n      评审 concern #11 (tautology) 被彻底 refuted。A3 假设强化：DIF removal 仍然比 random 显著\n      (z=-9.5)，但远小于 naive heuristics——这就是 \"DIF items carry signal but are NOT the most\n      ranking-defining items\" 的 precise meaning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Circularity Ablation (Ranking Disruption by Removal Strategy)\"\n        columns: [strategy, n_items, ρ_full_vs_subset, disruption_z, overlap_with_DIF_pct]\n        rows:\n          - [random_baseline, 3918, 0.9985, 0, \"—\"]\n          - [DIF_C_removal, 3918, 0.9970, -9.5, 100]\n          - [high_discrimination, 3918, 0.9958, -16, 22.1]\n          - [high_variance, 3918, 0.9831, -108, 41.3]\n          - [accuracy_gap, 3918, 0.9712, -157, 62.6]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 5: Bar chart of disruption z-scores by removal strategy. DIF is closest to random despite 62.6% overlap with accuracy-gap. Demonstrates MH conditioning effect.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Key evidence for Claim 4 sub-finding 2. In best tier, this analysis demonstrates deep\n      methodological understanding. The 62.6% overlap + 16× disruption gap is the \"aha moment\"\n      that convinces reviewers MH-DIF is doing something genuinely different from naive accuracy\n      comparison. Tautology concern fully resolved.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_021: Non-Uniform DIF Robustness (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"nonuniform_dif_robustness\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_021\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic Regression DIF on 9 subjects (1,787 items). Test MH's uniform-only\n      assumption and quantify non-uniform DIF prevalence.\n    expected_results:\n      n_subjects: 9\n      n_items: 1787\n      mh_lr_concordance: 0.921\n      nonuniform_dif_significance_pct: 38.7\n      nonuniform_dif_effect_size_pct: 24.8\n      mh_conservative_estimate_confirmed: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，LR-DIF 的 92.1% concordance with MH 证明 MH classification 对 uniform DIF\n      是 robust。38.7% non-uniform DIF at significance threshold, 24.8% at |β_interaction|≥0.5\n      证明 MH 结构性地 underestimates instability——31% 是 conservative estimate。\n      评审 concern #9 (only uniform DIF) 被直接回应：\"our 31% uniform-only estimate is conservative;\n      including non-uniform DIF raises it to ~25% additional items.\" Best 档下评审接受 caveat\n      (LR used within-subject matching vs MH's cross-benchmark) 并同意使用 24.8% (effect-size\n      controlled) 而非 38.7% (significance-only)。这展现方法论 conservatism。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S8: Non-Uniform DIF (Logistic Regression)\"\n        columns: [metric, value]\n        rows:\n          - [MH_LR_C_concordance, \"92.1%\"]\n          - [non_uniform_DIF_significance, \"38.7%\"]\n          - [non_uniform_DIF_effect_size, \"24.8% (|β_int|≥0.5)\"]\n          - [n_subjects_tested, 9]\n          - [n_items_tested, 1787]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S8: MH classification vs LR classification confusion matrix. 92.1% concordance for ETS C class.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Appendix robustness check. In best tier, the key message is \"31% is conservative\" —\n      this flips a potential weakness (MH is old/simple) into a strength (our estimate is\n      a lower bound). The 24.8% effect-size-controlled figure is the one used in the paper text.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_022: Model Independence (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"model_independence\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_022\"\n    description: >\n      Graduated de-duplication: cap models per family at K={1,2,5,10,20}. Compare C% at\n      each cap vs random subsample of same size. Test whether family structure inflates DIF.\n    expected_results:\n      k20_n_models: 447\n      k20_c_pct: 29.1\n      k20_random_c_pct: 30.9\n      k10_c_pct: 24.3\n      k10_random_c_pct: 27.5\n      k5_n_models: 146\n      k5_c_pct: 11.7\n      k5_random_c_pct: 16.9\n      k1_n_models: 33\n      k1_c_pct: 0.17\n      k1_note: \"underpowered (N<80)\"\n      family_inflates_c_pct: false\n      dif_at_every_cap_leq_random: true\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，graduated de-duplication 是对 concern #10 (model non-independence) 的决定性回应。\n      在每个 cap K 下，family-capped C% ≤ random subsample C%。K=20: 29.1% vs 30.9%,\n      K=5: 11.7% vs 16.9%。Family structure 不仅不 inflate C%，反而 slightly reduces it。\n      K=1 (33 families) 的 0.17% 是 underpowered (N<80) 导致 MH test 无法达到 significance，\n      不是 DIF 消失。评审接受 graduated design 的 methodological rigor——不是 cherry-pick 一个 K，\n      而是 show monotonic trend。A1 假设强化：31.3% 是 genuine 的，not an artifact of model duplication。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table S9: Model Independence — Graduated De-duplication\"\n        columns: [cap_K, N_models, C_pct_family_cap, C_pct_random_subsample, delta]\n        rows:\n          - [20, 447, 29.1, 30.9, -1.8]\n          - [10, 283, 24.3, 27.5, -3.2]\n          - [5, 146, 11.7, 16.9, -5.2]\n          - [2, 66, 2.1, 5.8, -3.7]\n          - [1, 33, 0.17, 0.84, \"-0.67 (underpowered)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig S9: Paired line plot of C% (family-capped vs random subsample) at each K. Family-capped consistently at or below random.\"\n    analysis: >\n      Resolves concern #10. In best tier, the graduated design is elegant — it shows the\n      relationship between sample independence and DIF detection is not driven by model\n      family inflation. The \"family C% ≤ random C%\" pattern at every K is stronger than\n      just showing \"similar\" — it shows family structure, if anything, suppresses DIF detection.\n\n  # ============================================================\n  # plan_023: Item Characterization (DONE)\n  # ============================================================\n  - name: \"item_characterization\"\n    plan_id: \"plan_023\"\n    description: >\n      Characterize DIF-C items by difficulty, discrimination, domain distribution, and\n      DIF direction. Key finding: difficulty×direction interaction.\n    expected_results:\n      difficulty_cohen_d: -0.247\n      discrimination_cohen_d: 0.230\n      domain_chi2_p: 0.32\n      domain_uniformly_distributed: true\n      direction_focal_favoring_pct: 43.9\n      direction_reference_favoring_pct: 56.1\n      difficulty_direction_rho: -0.597\n      hardest_decile_focal_favoring_pct: 88.7\n      easiest_decile_reference_favoring_pct: 96.2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Best 档下，plan_023 是 Claim 4 的 surprise finding 升华全文。difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597\n      揭示了一个系统性 pattern：hardest-decile DIF-C items 88.7% favor 2024 models（capability\n      improvement concentrates on hard items），easiest-decile 96.2% favor 2023 models（easy items'\n      difficulty structure erodes across generations）。这从纯粹描述性的 \"31% are unstable\" 升级为\n      mechanistic story：\"which items changed and in what direction tells us about the nature of\n      capability improvement.\" A5 假设成立：difficulty×direction 作为 'capability improvement\n      concentrates on hard items' 的 mechanistic story 引起评审共鸣。DIF-C items moderately harder\n      (d=-0.247) 和 higher discrimination (d=0.230) 是 sensible——functionally changing items 倾向于\n      是更有区分度的 items。Domain uniformity (χ² p=0.32) 证明 instability 不 cluster 在特定领域——\n      这是 cross-domain phenomenon，strengthening generalizability。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Item Characterization of DIF-C Items\"\n        columns: [property, DIF_C_mean, non_DIF_mean, Cohen_d, p_value]\n        rows:\n          - [difficulty_p, 0.58, 0.65, -0.247, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [discrimination_rpbis, 0.34, 0.28, 0.230, \"<0.001\"]\n          - [domain_distribution, \"uniform\", \"uniform\", \"χ²_p=0.32\", \"—\"]\n      - name: \"Table 8: Difficulty × DIF Direction Interaction\"\n        columns: [difficulty_decile, n_DIF_C, pct_focal_favoring, pct_reference_favoring]\n        rows:\n          - [1_easiest, 287, 3.8, 96.2]\n          - [2, 312, 8.3, 91.7]\n          - [5_median, 401, 38.2, 61.8]\n          - [9, 478, 79.1, 20.9]\n          - [10_hardest, 512, 88.7, 11.3]\n          - [overall, 3918, 43.9, 56.1]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Fig 6: Stacked bar chart of DIF direction by difficulty decile. Clear gradient from 96.2% reference-favoring (easiest) to 88.7% focal-favoring (hardest). ρ=-0.597 annotation.\"\n      - \"Fig 7: Scatter plot of item difficulty vs Δ_MH, color-coded by direction. Strong negative trend visible.\"\n    analysis: >\n      The crown jewel of the paper in best tier. difficulty×direction ρ=-0.597 transforms the\n      paper from \"we found instability\" to \"we understand what drives it.\" This is the finding\n      that makes reviewer #3 write \"interesting and novel\" in their review. The mechanistic\n      story (hard items improve, easy items erode) connects to the broader ML narrative about\n      capability scaling — it's the kind of finding that ML researchers can immediately relate to\n      their own experience with model training. Domain uniformity adds confidence that this is\n      a general phenomenon, not an artifact of specific knowledge domains.\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ff7feff5-12f0-4f3d-8a05-edb61f233b1a","total_cost_usd":0.95806275,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42831,"cache_read_input_tokens":183939,"output_tokens":15537,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42831,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":